      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T13:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have a custom handler for ssh channels defined in the test. It accepts all channels and immediately closes it. This should mean that we don\u0027t depend on the test worker setup very much except that it needs to have /etc/services or the OS equivalent populated with the ssh service which should not require actually running the ssh service.\n\nI also tried to manually insert a service in the service file /etc/services but that usually requires root and so that was not easily done.\n\nThe current setup is as hermetic as I could figure out.",
      "parentUuid": "a5a9ce96_aa83bc3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 41,
